## A. blocked-rail pair — `-demoMode -corral458HerdScenario`

The demo fleet's global blocked rail carries `demo-garden-agent` (chestnut, breed 2 = draft,
blocked) — the affected pose, static (blocked horses are standstill, so the frames are
clock-independent). Per arm (`base`, `head`), all exits 0:

    xcrun simctl install   <udid> <arm app>                     -> 0  (evidence-install-<arm>.log)
    xcrun simctl terminate <udid> com.corral.fleetnotifier      -> (no-op if not running)
    xcrun simctl launch    <udid> com.corral.fleetnotifier \
        -demoMode -corral458HerdScenario                        -> 0  (evidence-launch-<arm>.log)
    xcrun simctl io        <udid> screenshot herd-<arm>-demo-N.png  (N = 1..3, 1.1 s apart)
                                                                -> 0 each (evidence-shots.exit)

## B. working-draft paddock pair — `-demoMode -corralDemoMultiHostBoardEvidence -corral458HerdScenario`

The multi-host demo seed's first paddock (`demo-atlas`) carries `demo-atlas-worker` — dun,
breed 2 = draft, **working** — drawn in the paddock, so nothing overlays its fetlocks. Same
install/launch/screenshot sequence per arm, all exits 0:

    xcrun simctl install <udid> <arm app>                       -> 0  (draft-<arm>-install.log)
    xcrun simctl launch  <udid> com.corral.fleetnotifier \
        -demoMode -corralDemoMultiHostBoardEvidence -corral458HerdScenario
                                                                -> 0  (draft-<arm>-launch.log)
    xcrun simctl io <udid> screenshot draft-<arm>-N.png         -> 0 each (draft-shots.exit)

Both horses' identities follow the app's name-derived axes (`HorseIdentity(name:)`,
